 "capsule": "Consolidated after William the Conqueror's victory at Hastings in 1066, Norman England was reorganized around a transplanted continental feudal aristocracy, extensive castle-building, and the sweeping 1086 land survey recorded in Domesday Book. Succession disputes among William's descendants erupted into the civil war known as the Anarchy (1135–1154) between King Stephen and Empress Matilda, resolved by installing the Angevin Henry II, whose reign extended Anglo-Norman power into Ireland with the 1169 invasion.",
